---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Scene from '../components/Scene.astro';
import DownloadLink from '../components/DownloadLink.astro';
import { url } from '../data/site';
import { releases } from '../data/releases';
---
<Layout title="Downloads & installation | ZBK" theme="nacht">
  <section class="page-intro wrap"><p class="eyebrow">YOUR NEXT ROUND STARTS HERE</p><h1>LOAD IN.<br /><em>HOLD OUT.</em></h1><p class="lede">Playable worlds and the tools to build your own.<br />For Minecraft Java Edition {releases.minecraft}.</p></section>
  <section class="downloads-section wrap" id="nacht"><div class="section-heading"><h2>PLAYABLE <em>MAPS.</em></h2><span class="eyebrow">WORLD + RESOURCE PACK</span></div><article class="download-panel"><Scene name="nacht-exterior" alt="Nacht der Untoten bunker" /><div><p class="eyebrow">NACHT DER UNTOTEN</p><h3>BACK TO THE BUNKER.</h3><p>The world and resource pack are separate files. Install both for the complete ZBK experience.</p><dl class="requirements"><div><dt>Edition</dt><dd>Java</dd></div><div><dt>Minecraft</dt><dd>{releases.minecraft}</dd></div><div><dt>Release</dt><dd>{releases.version || 'Details coming soon'}</dd></div><div><dt>Required</dt><dd>Matching resource pack</dd></div></dl><div class="actions"><DownloadLink href={releases.nachtWorld} label="Nacht world" /><DownloadLink href={releases.resourcePack} label="Resource pack" /></div><a class="text-link" href="#install">How to install ↓</a></div></article><div class="upcoming-release" id="de"><span class="status-tag">IN DEVELOPMENT</span><strong>DER EISENDRACHE</strong><a href={url('#der-eisendrache')}>Follow the build ↗</a></div></section>
  <section class="downloads-section wrap" id="kit"><div class="section-heading"><h2>BUILD YOUR <em>OWN.</em></h2><span class="eyebrow">ZOMBIES BUILD KIT</span></div><div class="kit-downloads"><article><span class="eyebrow">START WITH A WORLD</span><h3>ZBK STARTER WORLD</h3><p>A starting point for your own Zombies map. Pair it with the matching resource pack.</p><DownloadLink href={releases.starterWorld} label="Starter world" /></article><article><span class="eyebrow">BRING YOUR OWN WORLD</span><h3>ZBK DATAPACK</h3><p>Add the kit to your own build. Install the datapack in the world and enable its resource pack.</p><DownloadLink href={releases.datapack} label="ZBK datapack" /></article><article><span class="eyebrow">THE LOOK. THE SOUND.</span><h3>ZBK RESOURCE PACK</h3><p>The models, textures, sounds, and HUD that bring it all together. Required for maps and the kit.</p><DownloadLink href={releases.resourcePack} label="Resource pack" /></article></div></section>
  <section class="installation wrap" id="install"><p class="eyebrow">DOWNLOAD TO FIRST ROUND</p><h2>THREE STEPS.<br /><em>THEN SURVIVE.</em></h2><ol class="install-steps"><li><span>01</span><div><h3>INSTALL THE WORLD</h3><p>Extract the world archive. Move the folder containing <code>level.dat</code> into your Minecraft <code>saves</code> folder. Make sure it isn't nested inside an extra folder.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><h3>ENABLE THE RESOURCE PACK</h3><p>In Minecraft, open Options → Resource Packs → Open Pack Folder. Copy the matching resource-pack ZIP there, then enable it in the game.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><h3>ENTER THE OUTBREAK</h3><p>Launch Minecraft Java {releases.minecraft}, open the world from Singleplayer, and use the map's spawn menu to start. Keep a backup before updating a world.</p></div></li></ol><a class="text-link" href={url('tutorials/#troubleshooting')}>Need a hand? Open the field guide ↗</a></section>
</Layout>
